  "term": "Börjeson–Forssman–Lehmann syndrome",
  "definition": "Börjeson–Forssman–Lehmann syndrome is an X-linked recessive genetic condition caused by changes in the PHF6 gene. It is associated with severe intellectual disability and may also involve epilepsy, hypogonadism, hypometabolism, and obesity.",
